@host = http://localhost:5000
@ghostId = 64b7f0f0f0f0f0f0f0f0f0f0

# Reviews of one product (Part 5, checkpoint 1).
# Run from top to bottom. Before you start:
#   1. auth.http: run test A (admin) and then test B (Sara). They save adminToken, userToken, adminId.
#   2. products.http: run S1 to S4. They save managerToken.
# Access tokens last 15 minutes. If a test gives 401 when you expect something else, run A and B again.
# Run the whole file once. A second run starts with a new product, so it works again.


### R0. Setup: the manager creates a product for these tests -> 201, saves reviewProductId
POST {{host}}/api/v1/products
Authorization: Bearer {{managerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "review test chair",
  "price": 15000,
  "description": "A chair used only to test reviews",
  "category": "office",
  "company": "ikea",
  "inventory": 5
}

> {%
  client.global.set('reviewProductId', response.body.product.id)
%}

### R1. List the reviews of the new product, no token needed -> 200, empty list, total 0
GET {{host}}/api/v1/products/{{reviewProductId}}/reviews

### R2. The product has no rating yet -> 200, averageRating 0, numOfReviews 0
GET {{host}}/api/v1/products/{{reviewProductId}}

### R3. Write a review with no token -> 401
POST {{host}}/api/v1/products/{{reviewProductId}}/reviews
Content-Type: application/json

{ "rating": 5, "title": "Great", "comment": "I like it" }

### R4. A product that does not exist -> 404 "Product not found"
POST {{host}}/api/v1/products/{{ghostId}}/reviews
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "rating": 5, "title": "Great", "comment": "I like it" }

### R5. A broken product id -> 400 "Invalid value for _id"
POST {{host}}/api/v1/products/abc/reviews
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "rating": 5, "title": "Great", "comment": "I like it" }

### R6. Empty body -> 400 "Please provide rating" (the answer also lists the title and comment messages)
POST {{host}}/api/v1/products/{{reviewProductId}}/reviews
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{}

### R7. Rating 6 -> 400 "Rating must be from 1 to 5"
POST {{host}}/api/v1/products/{{reviewProductId}}/reviews
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "rating": 6, "title": "Great", "comment": "I like it" }

### R8. Rating 0 -> 400 "Rating must be from 1 to 5"
POST {{host}}/api/v1/products/{{reviewProductId}}/reviews
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "rating": 0, "title": "Great", "comment": "I like it" }

### R9. Rating with a decimal -> 400 "Rating must be a whole number from 1 to 5"
POST {{host}}/api/v1/products/{{reviewProductId}}/reviews
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "rating": 3.5, "title": "Great", "comment": "I like it" }

### R10. Rating is a word -> 400 (Mongoose's own message, a bit ugly but safe)
POST {{host}}/api/v1/products/{{reviewProductId}}/reviews
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "rating": "five", "title": "Great", "comment": "I like it" }

### R11. Title is an object -> 400 (same: ugly but safe)
POST {{host}}/api/v1/products/{{reviewProductId}}/reviews
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "rating": 5, "title": { "$gt": "" }, "comment": "I like it" }

### R12. Title with 101 letters -> 400 "Title must be at most 100 characters"
POST {{host}}/api/v1/products/{{reviewProductId}}/reviews
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "rating": 5, "title": "aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa", "comment": "I like it" }

### R13. Sara writes a review. The body also tries to set the writer and the product -> 201, both are ignored (the writer is Sara, the product is the one in the URL)
POST {{host}}/api/v1/products/{{reviewProductId}}/reviews
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "rating": 5,
  "title": "Great chair",
  "comment": "Very comfortable, I use it every day",
  "user": "{{adminId}}",
  "product": "{{ghostId}}"
}

> {%
  client.global.set('saraReviewId', response.body.review.id)
%}

### R14. The product now shows the rating -> 200, averageRating 5, numOfReviews 1
GET {{host}}/api/v1/products/{{reviewProductId}}

### R15. Sara writes a second review for the same product -> 409 "You already reviewed this product"
POST {{host}}/api/v1/products/{{reviewProductId}}/reviews
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "rating": 1, "title": "Changed my mind", "comment": "Trying to review twice" }

### R16. The manager writes a review (a manager is a normal customer here) -> 201
POST {{host}}/api/v1/products/{{reviewProductId}}/reviews
Authorization: Bearer {{managerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "rating": 4, "title": "Good", "comment": "Good for the price" }

> {%
  client.global.set('managerReviewId', response.body.review.id)
%}

### R17. The product shows the new average -> 200, averageRating 4.5, numOfReviews 2
GET {{host}}/api/v1/products/{{reviewProductId}}

### R18. The admin writes a review -> 201
POST {{host}}/api/v1/products/{{reviewProductId}}/reviews
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "rating": 4, "title": "Fine", "comment": "Does what it should" }

### R19. Average of 5, 4 and 4 is 4.33 -> 200, averageRating 4.3 (not rounded up to 5), numOfReviews 3
GET {{host}}/api/v1/products/{{reviewProductId}}

### R20. List the reviews -> 200, three reviews, newest first (admin, manager, Sara), each with the writer's name, total 3
GET {{host}}/api/v1/products/{{reviewProductId}}/reviews

### R21. Second page of two -> 200, one review (Sara's), count 1, total 3, totalPages 2
GET {{host}}/api/v1/products/{{reviewProductId}}/reviews?limit=2&page=2

### R22. Page 0 -> 400 "page must be a whole number from 1 to 100000"
GET {{host}}/api/v1/products/{{reviewProductId}}/reviews?page=0

### R23. Reviews of a product that does not exist -> 404 "Product not found"
GET {{host}}/api/v1/products/{{ghostId}}/reviews

### R24. The admin deletes the product -> 200 "Product removed" (its three reviews are deleted too)
DELETE {{host}}/api/v1/products/{{reviewProductId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### R25. The reviews of the deleted product -> 404 "Product not found"
GET {{host}}/api/v1/products/{{reviewProductId}}/reviews
